    "Footer.startEating" : {
      "comment" : "Primary action on the .complete footer card: opens the eating window. Replaces the literal key 'Start eating window'. The English source drops the word 'window' for two independent reasons. First, consistency: eight of the ten locales already say only 'start eating' (uk 'Почати їсти', de 'Essen starten', es 'Empezar a comer', fr 'Passer à table', pl 'Zacznij jeść', zh 开始进食, ar ابدأ الأكل, ja 食事を開始) — English was the outlier, and every translator had silently corrected it. Only ko keeps the window in the name, because 식사 시간 is the established Korean term. Second, the concept is named twice on the same card anyway: the stat directly above the button reads WINDOW OPENS. Layout: 153.3pt -> 90.1pt, which takes the English primary off the 0.766 scale it had been sitting on at xxLarge and back to 1.000.",
