    "Pro.restoredDone" : {
      "comment" : "Primary button on the paywall in the .restored state (PaywallView.swift:229) - the screen shown after a restore succeeds. This is the primary action of a RESULT PANEL, not the dismissal token of an alert: the screen keeps its title, its badge and its check-marks, and this button sits in the same full-width primaryAction slot (OfferButton) that carries Buy and Restore in the other states. Use the locale's Done lexeme, the word the platform puts on the primary of a finished result panel, and NOT its OK lexeme - Apple separates the two deliberately and ships both in one file (REDEEM_SUCCESS_DONE_BUTTON = Done, REDEEM_OK_BUTTON = OK). Not a close/dismiss lexeme either. Split off the shared literal key 'Done'; the other half is PlanEditor.confirm. Values are unchanged by this split - the key exists so the two surfaces can never drift into each other again.",
